<title>COLOMBIA: Colombia raises '96 coffee crop estimate.</title>
<headline>Colombia raises '96 coffee crop estimate.</headline>
<dateline>BOGOTA 1996-10-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>The head of Colombia's powerful National Coffee Growers Federation said he had revised his estimate of the crop in the 1996 calendar year to 11.7 million 60-kilo bags from a previous estimate of 11 million bags.</p>
<p>Jorge Cardenas, the country's veteran coffee czar, announced the upward revision in remarks to reporters late Thursday after an emergency meeting of the policy-making National Coffee Growers Committee.</p>
<p>The meeting was called to discuss measures aimed at averting a industrywide crisis because of low world prices and the recent strengthening of Colombia's peso currency, which has eroded the value of export revenues.</p>
<p>--Juan Guillermo Londono, Bogota newsroom, 571 610 7944</p>
